BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of American Roots Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260422T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260422T210000
UID:260417HnHRUNAVm0K6fLAPXypWlw
DESCRIPTION:Walker Creek Music Camp Presents Teacher Concert Series IV Ben
 efit Concert Celebrating American Roots Music The evening will feature the
 se outstanding faculty and alumni performing bluegrass\, old-time\, jazz\,
  and swing: Walker Creek All-Stars A "supergroup" of current and former in
 structors featuring: Yoseff Tucker \\(guitar\\)\, Tod Livingston \\(dobro\
 \)\, Bethany Raine Sorkey \\(bass\\)\, Paul Shelasky \\(fiddle\\)\, Ryan B
 reen \\(banjo\\)\, and Tom Bekeny \\(mandolin\\). Hildaland A duo blending
  Scottish and American traditions featuring fiddler Louise Bichan and mand
 olin virtuoso Ethan Setiawan. Pacific Drive A high-energy bluegrass band f
 ormed at Walker Creek Music Camp featuring Dana Frankel\, David Thiessen\,
  Jesse Fichman\, Helen Foley\, and Sam Reed. alker Creek Music Camp Founde
 d in 2013\, Walker Creek Music Camp is a California nonprofit dedicated to
  teaching\, preserving\, and celebrating American roots music. The camp of
 fers world-class instruction for students of all ages and hosts sessions t
 wice each year at Walker Creek Ranch Conference Center. The camp's Music &
  More \\(M&M's\\) youth program provides tuition-free instruction for chil
 dren ages 6-13\, along with scholarships and work-trade opportunities that
  help make music education accessible to all. The concert supports Walker 
 Creek Music Camp's mission to provide world-class music education and expa
 nd access to traditional roots music through classes\, youth programs\, an
 d scholarships. More information:  walkercreekmusiccamp.org
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/an-evening-of-american-roots-music/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
