BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The 9th Annual We the Future Social Justice Conference!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T143000
UID:260415IG2aoNJS0E6EWcvWgPp-lQ
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 24\, 2026\,  from 9:00am – 2:30pm\, Santa Ro
 sa Junior College and North Bay Organizing Projects invites you to attend 
 the 9th Annual We the Future Social Justice Conference! \n\nThis year’s
  conference centers the truth that joy and resistance are not opposites 
 — they are intertwined liberatory practices. Joy fuels resistance. Resis
 tance protects the conditions for joy. Together\, they form the heartbeat 
 of collective liberation.\n\nWe the Future 2026 calls us to gather\, learn
 \, heal\, create\, and act together — rooting in joy\, practicing resist
 ance\, and shaping liberatory futures in community. We are thrilled to wel
 come this year’s keynote speaker\, Prisca Dorcas Mojica Rodríguez\, who
  is a writer\, organizer\, and public intellectual whose work centers the 
 lived experiences of undocumented and formerly undocumented Latine communi
 ties.\n\nCome and explore through three pathways: Educate. Activate. Creat
 e. \n\nSave your spot and register to attend this free event at **wethefu
 ture.santarosa.edu.**
LOCATION:Petaluma SRJC
URL:https://wethefuture.santarosa.edu/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Olive Oil Challah Demo at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T120000
UID:260414FqN_pgH_q0ir6BMq7S-5KA
DESCRIPTION:Learn to mix\, knead\, braid\, and bake olive oil challah. Ste
 phanie Rosenbaum Klassen will demonstrate her version of this rich\, soft 
 egg bread made with our estate-grown olive oil and local honey—perfect f
 or any celebration. We’ll also include a recipe (and taste) of Challah F
 rench Toast with Apple Cider Syrup.\n\nThe experience begins with a leisur
 ely walk through our orchard to the Apple Cottage\, where the demo takes p
 lace surrounded by the beauty of the farm. Afterward\, guests will ride ba
 ck to the Farm Shop aboard our beloved apple-themed trolley.\n\nStephanie 
 Rosenbaum Klassen is Gold Ridge Organic Farms' Farm Shop lead\, bringing y
 ears of experience as a cookbook author\, teacher\, and food writer. Her a
 cclaimed books include A Little Taste of San Francisco\, World of Doughnut
 s\, and Honey from Flower to Table. Her work has appeared in The New York 
 Times\, San Francisco Chronicle\, Edible publications\, and more.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/600726/oliv
 e-oil-challah-demo-with-stephanie-rosenbaum-klassen
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon on Monday - Duran Duran Tribute
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T235800
UID:2604149jFYfBUXgUOC7QpTulaRqg
DESCRIPTION:New Moon on Monday is the true fan's tribute to Duran Duran. 
 As dedicated students of DD’s iconic sound and style\, this band is no c
 heap imitation. \n\nInstead\, it’s a group built on honouring these pio
 neers of the New Romantic era and the British Invasion of MTV. \n\nWith p
 assion and precision\, New Moon performs an impressive array of the catalo
 gue\, from massive hits like “Girls on Film” to beloved lesser-knowns 
 such as “Hold Back the Rain.” \n\n An often neglected aspect of Dura
 n tributes\, however\, is the fashion! New Moon’s meticulous wardrobe a
 nd stage effects reflect the major influence of designers such as Vivienne
  Westwood on Duran's overall aesthetic. You won’t see cheap wigs or chea
 p digs when New Moon hits the stage.\n\nNew Moon on Monday is the premiere
  Duran tribute: capturing the fire\, the charm\, the style and the craft 
 - and bringing it to you.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://wl.eventim.us/event/new-moon-on-monday-duran-duran-tribute/684
 651?afflky=MysticTheatre
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Especies de Sonoma: Aves (Sonoma Species: Birds) en Español
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T140000
UID:260412jcOPaOYIwUixufXKSx7NJA
DESCRIPTION:Un programa de "Rutas y Aventuras" presentado por Jack London 
 Park Partners y "Senderos Naturales" por el Sonoma Ecology Center.\n\nEn e
 sta caminata\, guiada en español\, aprenderá a utilizar la aplicación M
 erlin Bird ID en el Parque Histórico Estatal Jack London. En primavera\, 
 este parque cobra vida con una multitud de especies de aves que llegan par
 a construir sus nidos y buscar alimento\, abarcando desde golondrinas y co
 libríes hasta halcones y búhos. ¡Venga a descubrir las maravillosas ave
 s que habitan en el Valle de Sonoma!\n\nEste taller se centrará en:\n\n
 • Cómo utilizar Merlin Bird ID para identificar aves mediante su canto 
 y fotografías\n\n• Consejos básicos para la observación de la natural
 eza y para mejorar sus habilidades de identificación\n\n• Información 
 general sobre las aves\, plantas y animales comunes que se encuentran en e
 l Valle de Sonoma y el Condado de Sonoma\n\n• Cómo estas aplicaciones a
 yudan a los científicos y a los parques a proteger la biodiversidad local
 \n\nEste programa es ideal para principiantes\, familias\, amantes de la n
 aturaleza y cualquier persona con una mente curiosa. No se requiere experi
 encia previa. Avanzaremos paso a paso y habrá tiempo suficiente para hace
 r preguntas y realizar prácticas guiadas. Se trata de una caminata fácil
  con una pendiente moderada.\n\nPuede encontrar información adicional y r
 ealizar su inscripción en https://jacklondonpark.com/events/aves/.\n\nAco
 mpáñenos nuevamente el 25 de abril para poner en práctica sus nuevas ha
 bilidades e identificar plantas y animales en el Parque Estatal Sugarloaf 
 Ridge\, con la ayuda de iNaturalist. Regístrese en https://sec.regfox.com
 /senderos26-cnc \\(se aplica un depósito de $5 para adultos\\).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/especies-de-sonoma-aves
 -sonoma-species-birds-en-espa-ol/18510158/2026-04-24T09
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nocturnal Biodiversity Crawl City Nature Challenge 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T200000
UID:260412a-7oldnAzkmrnUpty_TwtQ
DESCRIPTION:What is out after dark? Certified California Naturalist
  Erik Hanson of EH Outings takes us on a nighttime bioblitz al
 ong Lower Bald Mountain and Creekside Nature Trails in search of
  nocturnal biodiversity as part of City Nature Challenge weekend.
  Smartphones with the iNaturalist app will be our main tool\, b
 ut those lacking phones are also welcome to participate. If you
  haven’t used iNaturalist\, or haven’t made an observation fo
 r a while\, this is your chance – just make sure to load th
 e iNaturalist app on your phone before you arrive. \n\nMeet behi
 nd the Visitor Center. Tickets are $10 for general admission\, $
 5 for students\, youth (13-17 year olds)\, Sugarloaf members\, Su
 garloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free for children 7-12. **Tickets
  day-of on site are $15 and might not be available**. All chil
 dren under 18 must be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian
 . This outing is not for children under 7 years old. Tickets o
 n site will be $15 and might not be available. Wear appropriate
  footwear for slippery/rocky trails\, bring layers\, at least a 
 quart of water\, a flashlight or headlamp with red light capabil
 ity\, and of course\, a fully charged mobile phone or camera. P
 arking fees apply.\n\nThe 2026 City Nature Challenge runs from Ap
 ril 24 to 27. It’s a bioblitz-style friendly competition where
  "cities" are in a contest against each other to see who can 
 make the most observations of nature\, who can find the most sp
 ecies\, and who can engage the most people.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/nocturnalcrawl2026cnc
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Trashion" Print Lab: Tetra Pak & Milk Carton Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260424T193000
UID:260412WHQGcPmLV0-wjbNHQN5bng
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFriday\, April 24\, 2026 5:30 PM – 7:30 PM\n\nLo
 cation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: 
 Printmaking\, Sustainability\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n16\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\
 n\n$15\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$15\n\
 nIn honor of “Trashion Fashion” we are focusing on creative reuse\, an
 d sustainable printmaking! \n\nAbout the Class\n\nRoll up your sleeves an
 d join us for a special evening of “Trashion” Print Lab! Our mission i
 s to explore a creative arts technique socially with our community. Print 
 Lab is not a traditional class\, but an affordable art-making experience. 
 We welcome you to print\, play and experiment with an activity to create s
 omething unique in our printmaking studio!  In honor of “Trashion Fashi
 on” we are focusing on creative reuse\, and sustainable printmaking!  T
 etra Pak printmaking is an eco-friendly and accessible art technique that 
 repurposes used food and beverage cartons – like those for milk\, juice\
 , or broth\, as printing plates. It is a form of intaglio printmaking \\(s
 imilar to drypoint etching\\)\, where you scratch or “incise” a design
  into the carton’s inner foil or plastic lining to create a printable su
 rface. Carton printing is widely considered a highly sustainable alternati
 ve to traditional etching because it prioritizes creative reuse and non-to
 xic processes. Recycle\, repurpose and recreate! Learn how to turn garbage
  into beautiful prints! We will demonstrate how to draw\, scratch\, cut\, 
 ink and print carton surfaces on our presses with water-soluble etching in
 ks. Guests will leave with their own prints they create! We have plenty of
  cartons to share\, but we encourage guests to bring their own cleaned Tet
 ra Pak’s and milk cartons to use or donate to the printmaking studio. No
  printmaking experience is necessary. Light refreshments will be provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/trashion-print-lab-tetra-pa
 k-milk-carton-printing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
