BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Benicia & Vallejo Annual Demonstration Food Forest Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T160000
UID:260415ILfjRcCvFEqbM_ArYWfJ1w
DESCRIPTION:Tour demonstration food forests\, native plant\, pollinator an
 d community gardens!\n\nHave you ever seen a food forest? Are you interest
 ed in growing your own food or want to replace your lawn with a more susta
 inable landscape? Join our annual Food Forest Tour! Do not miss out on the
  chance to tour native plant\, pollinator\, local community gardens and ou
 r demonstration edible gardens fed by secondary water \\(roofwater and/or 
 laundry-to-landscape greywater system\\) in Benicia and Vallejo!\n\nLearn 
 simple techniques that you can apply to your own yard to create a vibrant\
 , food-producing ecosystem using water wisely.\n\nAsk our food forest keep
 ers questions\, enjoy the gardens\, be inspired and get ideas on how you c
 an work these design principles into your own yard!\n\nThis year we will b
 e partnering with CNPS Willis Linn Jepson Chapter to include Native Plant 
 Gardens on the tour.\n\nHow it will work:\n\nYou can choose to tour for th
 e whole day or for half a day on Saturday\, April 25\n\nBenicia Demonstrat
 ion Food Forest Gardens will be open 10-1 pm\n\nVallejo Demonstration Food
  Forest Gardens will be open 1-4 pm\n\nItinerary pickup and special events
 \n\n9-11 am: A detailed itinerary with garden locations will be distribute
 d at Avant Garden in Benicia \\(400 First St.\\) This itinerary will inclu
 de all of the demonstration food forest gardens in Benicia \\(open in the 
 morning\\) and Vallejo \\(open in the afternoon\\). There will be four nat
 ive plant gardens in Benicia and one in Vallejo\n\n12-1 pm: Itineraries fo
 r the Vallejo garden sites \\(open in the afternoon\\) will be available i
 n the front of the Global Center for Success building:1055 Azuar Dr\\(BLDG
  733\\) at Pollinator Pathway\n\nWe strongly encourage carpooling for ease
  of travel and for the company of \\(new or old\\) friends!\n\n$15 suggest
 ed donation at check-in\n\nall tour attendees will sign a waiver during it
 inerary pick up
LOCATION:Global Center for Success
URL:https://www.gvrd.org/2026-03-23-sustainable-solano-teen-cooking-camp-f
 arm-field-trip
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
