BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T000000
UID:2604161X5Fbe8n10S8iydOozib9w
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Balletto Vineyards
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108185970?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Petaluma Spring Antique Faire
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T160000
UID:260415PfB76f5jDkyf1EueTxSWfA
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a day of shopping and collecting in beautiful Down
 town Petaluma!\n\nAntique and collectible lovers throughout the Bay Area a
 re welcome to come\, browse and shop the 41st Annual Petaluma Antique Fair
 e this Spring on Sunday\, April 26\, 8 am to 4 pm set in one delightful an
 d relaxing setting of Downtown Petaluma.  Admission is free.\n\nThe Faire
  will be located on Kentucky Street\, Fourth Street\, in the A Street park
 ing lot\, and on Western Avenue.\n\n"The Bay Area's Premier Antique Center
 \," Historic Downtown Petaluma will transform into an antique marketplace.
  Amid the beautiful historic buildings\, one-of-a-kind stores\, an incredi
 ble array of restaurants and cafes\, guests can find an incomparable selec
 tion of affordable antiques from over 200 dealers. The show has a nice var
 iety of estate jewelry\, linens\, furniture\, art\, kitchenware\, vintage 
 décor\, books\, and all kinds of unusual collectibles to suit everyone's 
 budget.\n\nThis show attracts over 8\,000 discerning collectors as well as
  first-time buyers wishing to collect and invest in real antiques.\n\nVisi
 t PetalumaDowntown.com for more information!
LOCATION:Historic Downtown Petaluma
URL:https://petalumadowntown.com/antique-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
