BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Passport to Dry Creek Valley 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T160000
UID:260412nEYyZft5b0WlNqmhQfcZfA
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us and 25+ wineries per day for Passpo
 rt to Dry Creek Valley\, California’s Friendliest Wine + Food Festival!
  Travel throughout 16 X 2 idyllic miles and enjoy sun-soaked vineyards
 \, laughter amongst friends\, and unforgettable experiences in world-
 class wine\, food\, and musical entertainment!\n\nSingle-day passes ava
 ilable for a taste of the magic as well as weekend passes to soak
  it all in! Meet founders & winemakers\, taste award-winning wines 
 and hyper-local foodie bites\, and enjoy live music and DJ beats! Plus
 \, full access to insider perks all weekend long.\n\nThe perfect blend of 
 tradition and innovation\, Dry Creek Valley is where serious wine is craft
 ed in a delightfully relaxed environment. It honors the legendary families
  who have been here for generations\, and is as much about the community a
 s it is about the land and the wine.\n\nYou’re supporting the legacy of 
 Dry Creek Valley's agriculture\, story and our non-profit organization –
  celebrating the valley\, its wineries\, farmers\, grape growers and commu
 nity!\n\nExperience soil to sip – taste the land. Looks good in the glas
 s. Even better when you taste it.\n\nWhether it’s your first year or one
  of many\, there is an immense amount to discover — and rediscover!
LOCATION:Dry Creek Valley AVA
URL:https://www.drycreekvalley.org/dcv-passport/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sugarloaf New Volunteer Orientation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260426T150000
UID:260412_cbL8UKH6ECVXhWQwjvlSw
DESCRIPTION:When you join Sugarloaf's 200+ member volunteer communi
 ty\, you gain access to a whole new appreciation for your local
  State Park. Make meaningful connections with fellow volunteers\,
  learn new skills\, enjoy time outdoors in a beautiful setting\,
  and play an integral role in keeping Sugarloaf Ridge State Par
 k open and accessible for everyone.\n\n Join us at our next vol
 unteer orientation Sunday April 26\, 2026 from 1:00- 3:00 pm to 
 learn what it takes to steward a state park! We'll cover the h
 istory of Sugarloaf\, how Sonoma Ecology Center operates the park
 \, and the various volunteer opportunities available. Beyond the 
 mandatory initial orientation\, trainings and docent enrichment act
 ivities will take place periodically\, depending on your interests
  and role. \n\nHere are some of the vital ways that volunteers
  support Sugarloaf's operations:\n\nServe as docents at the Visito
 r Center\n\nDirect visitors at the entrance kiosk\n\nAssist with d
 ata collection and entry\, like our extensive Critter Cam wildlif
 e tracking project\n\nAid project research and grant-writing\n\nWork
  on trail and park maintenance projects\n\nFacilitate special even
 ts and parking\n\nSpanish/English literacy and conversational fluenc
 y is a plus
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/ap2026orientation
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
