BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SRJC Fashion Studies Fashion Show "The Equinox"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T203000
UID:260412XjRmVF3Svke28f2YK6ZVDw
DESCRIPTION:SRJC fashion program is proud to announce the annual student r
 un fashion show\, “The Equinox”.  The show will be held on Thursday\,
  April 30th\, 2026\,  SRJC Petaluma Campus Clocktower Plaza. This year’
 s students are ecstatic to reveal that this year’s show will be unique i
 n its production and scope. “We’re taking lighting and aesthetic immer
 sion to a whole new level\,” states the venue organizer\, Sebastian Faiv
 re. Show director\, Valeria Silva\, claims\, “This year's theme is so in
 teresting and different\, and I feel so excited to be working with so many
  creative individuals who are putting a lot into the show\, so it's defini
 tely going to be a must go!”\n\nThis year’s theme is The Equinox - the
  change of seasons\, the shift from dark winter to bright spring. The equi
 nox is representative of two opposites\, not in conflict\, but standing to
 gether in harmony. Hope and rebellion\, night and day\, darkness and radia
 nt color. The goal of the show is to celebrate a range of creative styles 
 that represent people\, with styles ranging from bubbly and poppy to dark 
 and alternative. \n\nThe show will feature the “Black and White” cont
 est\, where students are prompted to design a look by only using specific 
 black and white fabrics. Audience members will even be able to vote on the
 ir favorite look from the competition. The core show will consist of two a
 cts\, one representing darkness and one representing light. There will als
 o be a series of collections made from student designers\, who are all exc
 ited to showcase their vision\, hard work and techniques learned in fashio
 n studies. \n\nGeneral admission is $20\, and SRJC students are $10. Tick
 ets are available on Eventbrite.  Doors open at 7 PM\, with the show begi
 nning at 7:30. More information is available at the SRJC Fashion Studies W
 ebsite.
LOCATION:SRJC Petaluma Campus
URL:https://fashion.santarosa.edu/event/spring-2026-fashion-show
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T211500
UID:260412Jb7UkVfv5UamL7BztSlDyw
DESCRIPTION:Bring a flashlight and your sense of wonder as you e
 xplore the park after dark on Thursday\, April 30\, 6:15-9:15 pm
 . This **moderate-to-strenuous\, 4.2-mile** hike with approximately
  **800ft of elevation gain** heads up to the viewpoint on Vista
  Trail where we will see the moon rise over the Mayacamas and
  the sun set over Sonoma Valley. Not recommended for children u
 nder 7 years old.\n\n**Meet at the White Barn parking lot at le
 ast 10 minutes prior to 6:15pm** for a prompt departure. Tickets
  are $10 for general audiences\, $5 for students\, youth (13-17
  year olds)\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, a
 nd free for children 7-12 years old. All minors must be accompa
 nied by a parent or legal guardian. **You must register on this
  page to attend\; tickets on site will be $15 for all and mig
 ht not be available**. Bring your **flashlight**\, **at least a 
 quart of water**\, **extra layers** for the evening\, and if des
 ired\, a snack. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/ap2026moon
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
