BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: The Poetic Landscape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T180000
UID:260318SwTCJ0D-7UimjsWEVs1BcQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  3/13/26\n\n**APRIL EXHIBIT: THE 
 POETIC LANDSCAPE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  March 30  – April 26\, 2026\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, APRIL 4\, 2026\, 3-5 pm: Join us to meet KAREN MILL
 ER and PHYLLIS RAPP\;  celebrate the show and enjoy a poetry reading by f
 eatured guest\, Linda Loveland Reid\, gallery artist and published author.
   Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthly drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Karen Miller\,** presents **The Poetic Landscape\,** pa
 stel paintings that convey Miller’s personal experience in connecting wi
 th the intrinsic beauty of natural places. In these pieces\, color\, fluid
  shapes and rhythmic design combine to create an uplifting mood – a true
  poetic interlude.  Evoking a happy mood\, “Geyserville Sunflowers\,”
  turning to the sun by nature\, joyfully dance in its luminescence. By the
  river’s edge\, concentric reflections conjure a calm sense of wellbeing
  in “Fetch.”  The viewer feels welcomed by a warm embrace entering a 
 shaded secret spot in “September Trellis.”  Focused on local scenes\,
  these works truly hone in on the stunning landscape out our doors.  Mill
 er remarked “ As I contemplate the very real places of beauty surroundin
 g us\, I try to express my painterly response in hopes it will engender re
 cognition by the viewers.” \n\nMeet the artist: Miller will be hosting 
 the Gallery on March 30\, April 5 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n The Stai
 rway Smallworks Showcase features **Phyllis Rapp’s Magic Moments\,** a c
 ollection of watercolors that create an atmosphere that is both introspect
 ive and magical.  Familiar domestic scenes are transformed as humans inte
 ract with animals and birds in floral settings.  In “Silent Watcher” 
 the red-headed young woman’s green eyes lock onto ours as she stares ahe
 ad\, flanked by her avian companion.  Experiencing these works is a like 
 taking a mini-step on the wild side\, an exciting and fun experience.\n\nM
 eet the artist: Rapp will be hosting the Gallery on March 30 and April 10 
 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\
 , April 2\, 5 – 6 pm.  The theme for the 2026 kickoff event is Bouquets
  to Art.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is
  a community event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries p
 articipating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Cente
 r Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 
 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Con
 tact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What About Age? Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T180000
UID:260318H9KcZUNTo0qirgISzqTT9A
DESCRIPTION:*What About Age?* art exhibit has arrived in Marin County! Or
 iginally displayed at NYU’s Kimmel Windows\, this exhibit explores ageis
 m through contemporary art\, featuring works by both local youth and senio
 r artists.\n\n*What About Age?* is an art exhibit and educational initiat
 ive designed to challenge stereotypes about aging\, address ageism and soc
 ial isolation\, and promote intergenerational dialogue through the lens of
  art.\n\nIn partnership with Youth in Arts\, the exhibit features artworks
  by local youth and senior artists\, showcasing how age intersects with cr
 eativity\, identity\, and experience. Under the guidance of Youth in Arts\
 , these emerging and established artists work side by side to create colla
 borative pieces\, fostering meaningful connections between generations and
  reflecting the exhibit’s core message: art is ageless.\n\nThe exhibit a
 lso includes artwork panels by New York-based writer and illustrator Aubre
 y Hirsch\, first displayed at NYU’s Kimmel Windows and originally organi
 zed by Stacey Gordon\, NYU’s Program Director of Next Phase Adult Caregi
 ving and Retirement at Work Life.\n\nThe new exhibition will be on view at
  the Marin County Civic Center galleries from January 26 to May 6\, 2026. 
 Works will be displayed on the first and third floor exhibits\, Monday to 
 Friday from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m.\n\nThe *What About Age?* art exhibit is prese
 nted by Marin Cultural Association in partnership with Marin Community Fou
 ndation and Youth in Arts. Beyond the art exhibit\, the *What About Age?* 
 initiative offers programming\, led by Vivalon\, designed to challenge age
 ism and provide resources for Marin County's growing aging population.
LOCATION:Marin County Civic Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley of the Moon Music Festival Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T183000
UID:260315WlkBGxRzu0mnJS2PGCTYBw
DESCRIPTION:Jack London Park Partners welcomes the Valley of the Moon Musi
 c Festival\, Sonoma’s premier chamber music festival\, for an intimate c
 oncert on the second floor of the House of Happy Walls.   The program wi
 ll feature works by Antonín Dvořák\, performed by Valley of the Moon Mu
 sic Festival Directors - cellist Tanya Tomkins and pianist Eric Zivian - a
 longside critically acclaimed violinist Tien-Hsin Cindy Wu.   The event 
 begins with a wine reception at 5-5:30 p.m.\n\nAll proceeds benefit Jack L
 ondon Park Partners’ Education programs.\n\nThe Valley of the Moon Musi
 c Festival presents chamber music from across the centuries performed o
 n historical instruments and was recently voted Best Chamber Music Festiv
 al in the San Francisco Classical Voice Audience Choice Awards. Each su
 mmer\, the VMMF brings world-renowned artists and exceptional emerging mus
 icians to Sonoma for performances and training programs that foster artist
 ic excellence\, historical insight\, and deep community engagement.\n\nThi
 s year is VMMF’s 12th Season and events will run from July 9-26 in So
 noma.  For more information\, visit https://valleyofthemoonmusicfestival.
 org/. \n\nAccess to the venue is by stairs. For information about access\
 , call 707-938-5216.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/valley-of-the-moon-musi
 c-festival-concert/18329526/2026-04-30T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bring Back the Build Forum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T193000
UID:260314MmfbTe8t4USiasoptDN5_A
DESCRIPTION:Join the LIME Foundation for the Bring Back the Build Forum on
  April 30 from 5:00–7:30 PM at the Sonoma Clean Power Customer Center.\n
 \nThis event will bring together local contractors\, industry leaders\, an
 d workforce partners for an evening focused on the future of the trades. A
 ttendees will have the opportunity to network\, exchange ideas\, and discu
 ss emerging topics impacting the construction and skilled trades industrie
 s.\n\nTopics of discussion will include:\n\n• Workforce development and 
 building the next generation of skilled trades professionals\n\n• How AI
  and technology are impacting the industry\n\n• Using social media and d
 igital tools to grow your business\n\n• Industry trends and opportunitie
 s for collaboration\n\nGuests will also have the opportunity to tour Sonom
 a Clean Power’s facility and meet graduates from the LIME Foundation’s
  NextGen Trades Academy. These graduates are currently seeking employment 
 opportunities with local companies.\n\nWhether you're a contractor\, busin
 ess owner\, or industry professional\, this forum is a chance to connect\,
  learn\, and help strengthen the future workforce of our region.\n\nFood a
 nd drinks will be provided.\n\nPlease RSVP by April 23 at www.bringbackthe
 build.com\n\nIf you have any questions\, please contact ale@thelimefounda
 tion.org or call 707-532-5463.\n\nTo learn more about the LIME Foundation
 \, visit www.thelimefoundation.org.
LOCATION:Advanced Energy Center Sonoma
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/bring-back-the-build-fo
 rum/18326629/2026-04-30T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yotes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T000000
UID:26022467bO3upP5UC7QFGQZF-lvg
DESCRIPTION:Yotes combines his rich baritone vocals with an energetic deli
 very\, playing a mix of songs from 1950’s country\, 1980’s neo rockabi
 lly\, modern Americana\, and many genres and eras in between.  He mixes so
 ngs by Johnny Cash\, The Stray Cats\, The Blasters\, and Murder By Death w
 ith his own compositions.  Old favorites are interspersed with some of his
  favorite songs by friends and up-and-coming artists he’s met through th
 e years.\n\n \n\nOver the past fifteen years Yotes has developed his solo 
 show\, leaning on over two decades of performing experience in several ban
 ds ranging from high energy punk and rockabilly to soulful country\, folk\
 , and blues acts.  During that time his solo shows evolved from being a co
 nvenient testbed for new songs and exploring different styles to a full-ti
 me traveling act.  Yotes’s solo performances are tribute to the artists 
 and music that have influenced him\, a respectful nod to some of his favor
 ite contemporaries\, and an opportunity to share his own creations with li
 ve music fans everywhere!
LOCATION:JaM Cellars
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107905309?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
