DESCRIPTION:Pawsport Napa Valley 2026\n\nPURCHASE YOUR PAWSPORT HERE: http
 s://napahumane.org/events/pawsport/\n\nWhat Your Pawsport Unlocks: • One
  complimentary wine tasting per Pawsport holder at each participating wine
 ry • Access to a curated lineup of dog-friendly Napa Valley wineries\n\n
 How to Use Your Pawsport: • Your Pawsport is valid March 1–April 30\, 
 2026 with one tasting per person\, per winery • Be sure to check each wi
 nery’s hours and reservation requirements before visiting\, as many loca
 tions do require reservations\n\nYour Impact: Every Pawsport supports Napa
  Humane’s Power of Prevention—helping fund lifesaving spay and neuter 
 surgeries and preventive care that reduce overpopulation and prevent suffe
 ring. Together\, Pawsport supporters help make it possible to fund up to 2
 46 days of lifesaving surgery each year\, creating a lasting impact for an
 imal welfare in Napa County.\n\nReady to Sip for a Cause? Grab your Pawspo
 rt\, explore Napa Valley wineries\, and enjoy complimentary tastings all w
 hile helping protect pets through prevention-focused care. Don’t forget 
 to share your adventures using \\#PawsportNapaValley and by tagging @napah
 umane.\n\nThank you for helping make Napa Valley a more compassionate plac
 e for pets and the people who love them—we can’t wait to raise a glass
  with you this spring! 🐾🍷\n\nHave a question? Contact Gillian Ferro 
 at gferro@napahumane.org or by phone at \\(707\\) 255-8118 x205.
LOCATION:Napa Valley
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/pawsport-napa-valley-20
 26/18117345/2026-04-30T00
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Barbies & Bags Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T173000
UID:2602077Qt-EeeUQEuyJ8aRkiv9UA
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, February 15\, 2026 1:00 PM – 4:00 PM\n\
 nLocation\n\nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Level
 s\n\nKids\, Programming\, Sustainability\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\nAll Ages are wel
 come to attend Children under 16 must be accompanied by an adult\n\n$25 
 – One Bag or Doll Entry $40 – Two Bags or Dolls entryTransform plastic
  dolls and create upcycled bags from trash into unique art. Join our hands
 -on Trashion workshop for the Gallery 212 Exhibit and Auction.\n\nAbout th
 e Class\n\nThis hands-on workshop invites participants to rescue and reinv
 ent plastic dolls \\(Barbies\, Kens\, and dolls that are under 12 inches\\
 ) often destined for landfills\, where they can take 20 to 500 years to de
 compose. As part of Trashion Season\, join us for the beloved Gallery 212 
 Exhibit and Auction \\(April 3 – 25\\) where discarded materials are tra
 nsformed into small-scale works of art for a good cause. Together\, we’l
 l reclaim these forgotten figures and reimagine them as expressive\, one-o
 f-a-kind artworks for submission to the gallery exhibit and auction. New t
 his year: Bags! In addition to dolls\, we’re expanding the exhibit to in
 clude bags—think totes\, clutches\, cross bagsm fanny packs\, coin purse
 s\, and backpacks. Just like the Trashion runway\, the only rule is that y
 our piece must be made from unconventional materials and/or upcycled/used 
 textiles. Participants will have access to access to sewing machines\, hot
  glue guns\, irons\, hair dryers and other creative tools as well of a wid
 e selection of trash and upcycled materials to bring their vision to life.
  BYOT \\(Bring your own trash\\) is also welcome and encouraged! The works
 hop registration is your application fee to the gallery exhibit! Come play
 \, experiment\, and collaborate while contributing to a dynamic gallery ex
 hibit that raises funds for Sonoma Community Center programming through th
 e auction. It’s a joy to see your art find a new home—and to be part o
 f a creative community turning trash into treasure.\n\nThank you to Recolo
 gy Sonoma-Marin for donating Barbies & Dolls for our gallery exhibit every
  year.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/thursday-after-school/2026-
 01-08/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
