BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spanish and Cooking Class for Homeschoolers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T130000
UID:260401k6IjG-WbaEC9jiWMp3cBqw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nFridays\, April 10 – May 1\, 2026 10:00 AM – 1
 :00 PM\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories: Bilingual\, 
 Culinary Arts\, Kids\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n8-13\n\n$200 – Registration Cost\n
 \nStudents will learn Spanish vocabulary through doing art\, learning abou
 t Mexican culture\, and cooking over 4 weeks.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\nLearn
  basic Spanish greetings\, family\, animal\, and food vocabulary.\n\nExplo
 re Mexican culture through Lotería\, Día de los Muertos\, alebrijes\, pa
 pel picado\, and piñatas while creating related crafts.\n\nParticipate in
  games and activities that reinforce Spanish words and cultural traditions
 .\n\nLearn essential knife skills.\n\nLearn to cook the following deliciou
 s dishes: Seared black pepper ahi tuna with pico de gallo\, guacamole\, m
 ango habanero passion fruit salsa\, served in a tortilla chip. Cesar Salad
  with homemade croutons and dressing. Sopes with shredded beef and chicken
 .\n\nOn the final day\, students and their families will celebrate Día de
 l Niño together. The students will cook a special meal for their parents.
  Parents will be invited so we can all eat lunch together.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/spanish-and-cooking-homesch
 ool/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:KC Johns & Creed Fisher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T000000
UID:26033133QFHi8k8kyuUCLSvCLJLA
DESCRIPTION:If you listen to just a few tracks from his latest album\, you
  might think Creed Fisher was born with a guitar in his hand. One after an
 other his songs remain relevant today\, yet steeped with tradition classic
 s that everyone else already knows and you don’t want to miss. Clearly h
 e’s sharing his own stories\, with experiences that range from great vic
 tories to deep battle scars. \n\nFisher hails from Odessa\, TX\,  where hi
 s family’s roots trace back to his granddad\, who was highly involved in
  the oil game back in the fifties. However\, Fisher took on a different pa
 ssion when he started playing football at the age of 10\, which eventually
  led to the Minor Leagues for 9 years. \n\nBut\, as his football career ca
 me to a close\, Fisher also saw his marriage of twelve years come to an en
 d. It was at this point he decided to do some serious “soul searching”
 . Fisher tells us that the music simply “found him” during this time. 
 He picked up a guitar in 2010 and never let it go\; and after touring tire
 lessly for 4 years\, Fisher moved from West Texas to a small town outside 
 of San Antonio\, TX\, where he put together a new band\, and picked up whe
 re he left off.\n\nFisher’s second album "Ain't Scared To Bleed" went To
 p 30 on the ITunes Country charts and continues to be embraced by fans all
  around the world. When it came to his 3rd album "Rednecks Like Us" it was
  reviewed by Country Music People magazine and got 4 out of 5 stars. Here 
 is what they had to say...\n\n“Creed Fisher sings and writes with the co
 nfidence and authority of someone who has been at it for a hell of a lot l
 onger than 6 years. He is at his strongest on the ballads\, but tackles th
 e ‘angry redneck’ stuff just as well. There’s the odd moment when it
  can all get a bit crashy and loud for me\, but I’d say the same about H
 ank Jr. All things considered\, this is very impressive indeed and I’d l
 ike to see Creed Fisher go far.\n\nFriends and fans alike anxiously await 
 Creed Fisher’s release of his 4th album. There is no denying that Fisher
  is truly speaking from passion when it comes to his music. Fisher is the 
 guy you meet that you feel like you’ve known all your life and his music
  feels like the songs you’ve been singing since you first discovered mus
 ic. His lyrics\n\nare comfortable\; his story\, genuine\; his spirit\, hum
 ble and his talent\, undeniable.”\n\nCountry Music People Magazine \n\n-
  September 2016\n\n- Duncan Warwick \n\nRecently in 2021\, he’s been bac
 k on the road touring and will be looking forward to putting out new music
  for his fans.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107596370?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260501T170000
UID:260330e4LG1qyrr0yMCJiR45MS3w
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
