BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:11th Annual Duckhorn Vineyards Derby Party and Discussion Release
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T163000
UID:260120rNdYuMp4Gk-CyMHqJhuROQ
DESCRIPTION:This year\, we’re bringing the festivities to a new setting 
 at our sister property\, The Duckhorn Collection at Paraduxx\, where the l
 egacy continues in a fresh new way.\n\nSettle into the day with Southern-i
 nspired bites from our new Culinary team led by Chef Dominic Orsini and ou
 r signature wines poured across our lounge\, beneath the old oak tree\, an
 d beside the vines. From Duckhorn Vineyards to Goldeneye and beyond\, expe
 rience the spirit of The Duckhorn Collection as our home becomes yours for
  an afternoon of food\, wine\, and celebration.\n\nTradition and excellenc
 e unite as we debut the 16th vintage of The Discussion Red Blend—a wine 
 that embodies the ongoing dialogue of craftsmanship and connection in wine
 making. Be among the first to savor the new 2022 vintage of this Bordeaux-
 inspired blend while reveling in the excitement of the 152nd Kentucky Derb
 y!\n\nNo Derby celebration would be complete without our Best Dressed Comp
 etition\, inviting guests to showcase their finest race-day style—from b
 ig hats and fascinators to sport coats and bow ties. For those seeking a t
 ouch more elegance and ease\, The Winner’s Circle offers relaxed comfort
  and curated service. Enjoy personalized wine selections and thoughtful pa
 irings\, with a dedicated host ensuring you won’t miss a moment of the a
 ction. From start to finish\, it’s an effortless\, unforgettable Duckhor
 n Derby Day.\n\n\\*Derby-inspired attire suggested.\n\n\\*\\*Guests must b
 e 21 and over to attend. No pets are allowed at this event.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Al
 l ticket sales are non-refundable
LOCATION:The Duckhorn Collection at Paraduxx
URL:https://www.duckhorn.com/events/event-calendar/discussion-and-derby-pa
 rty
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Symphony - Shakespeare in Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260502T213000
UID:251217OygD9_-LXUecYFfzTcKVYw
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare in Music\n\nMay 2\, 3 & 4\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor\n\nClaire Huangci\,
  piano\n\nNicola Vann\, actor\n\nSAMUEL COLERIDGE-TAYLOR: Incidental Music
  from Othello\n\nWOLFGANG AMADEUS MOZART: Concerto No. 20 in D minor for P
 iano and Orchestra\, K. 466\n\nPYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Hamlet \\(Fantasy
  Overture\\) in F minor\, Opus 67\n\nPYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Romeo and J
 uliet \\(Fantasy Overture\\) in B minor\n\nStep into the world of Shakespe
 are’s dramatic\, enduring tales. Tchaikovsky’s passionate Romeo and Ju
 liet is a timeless and familiar classic\, while Coleridge-Taylor’s evoca
 tive Othello offers a compelling counterpoint for interpreting Shakespeare
  in music. Plus\, pianist Claire Huangci makes her Weill Hall debut with M
 ozart’s expressive Piano Concerto No. 20.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\
 , and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to 
 availability.\n\nPhoto by  Jean-Baptiste Millot
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
