DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T170000
UID:251217DhgOihH-xUuuyC-DW-yfJA
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare in Music\n\nMay 2\, 3 & 4\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor\n\nClaire Huangci\,
  piano\n\nNicola Vann\, actor\n\nSAMUEL COLERIDGE-TAYLOR: Incidental Music
  from Othello\n\nWOLFGANG AMADEUS MOZART: Concerto No. 20 in D minor for P
 iano and Orchestra\, K. 466\n\nPYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Hamlet \\(Fantasy
  Overture\\) in F minor\, Opus 67\n\nPYOTR ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Romeo and J
 uliet \\(Fantasy Overture\\) in B minor\n\nStep into the world of Shakespe
 are’s dramatic\, enduring tales. Tchaikovsky’s passionate Romeo and Ju
 liet is a timeless and familiar classic\, while Coleridge-Taylor’s evoca
 tive Othello offers a compelling counterpoint for interpreting Shakespeare
  in music. Plus\, pianist Claire Huangci makes her Weill Hall debut with M
 ozart’s expressive Piano Concerto No. 20.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\
 , and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to 
 availability.\n\nPhoto by  Jean-Baptiste Millot
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/shakespeare-in-music/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Head Over Heels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T161500
UID:250801KoKALz6YzkWCoNV131Y4wQ
DESCRIPTION:**A Kingdom at Risk\, a Beat That Won’t Quit\, and Love That
  Rules All!**\n\n***“It’s a feel good riot from start to finish.“* 
 — Jay Darcy\, Mancunion Media Group** \n\n**Get ready for a wild\, laugh
 -out-loud adventure with *HEAD OVER HEELS*—the electrifying musical come
 dy from the creative forces behind Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, Avenue Q\, 
 and Spring Awakening! Nominated for *Outstanding New Broadway Musical* in 
 2019 and powered by the chart-topping hits of the legendary all-female roc
 k band The Go-Go’s\, this high-energy show features beloved anthems like
  “We Got the Beat\,” “Our Lips Are Sealed\,” “Vacation\,” “H
 eaven is a Place on Earth\,” and “Mad About You.”**\n\n**Join a spir
 ited royal family on a whirlwind quest to save their kingdom from doom—o
 nly to realize that the key to their future isn’t written in fate\, but 
 in their own hearts. Packed with irresistible music\, over-the-top comedy\
 , and a whole lot of love\, *HEAD OVER HEELS* is a dazzling\, feel-good sp
 ectacle that will have you dancing in your seat!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays 
 & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours
 \, 15 mins including intermission\n\nThursdays Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult 
 $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $55.95\; Sen
 ior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices include fees(707) 523-4185**bo
 xoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:St Peter's Chapel Concert Series & VOENA present: Voices of Freedo
 m
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260503T161500
UID:260310SkFjxNFFY06dXx5HwpQhNw
DESCRIPTION:What does freedom sound like? Join VOENA for an electrifying a
 fternoon celebrating freedom of expression\, cultural identity\, and unity
  through song and rhythm. Voices of Freedom explores the many meanings of 
 freedom across cultures and histories\, featuring powerful performances fr
 om VOENA's diverse singers and global guest artists. This inspiring concer
 t is held in the stunning St. Peter's Chapel\, home to historic Tiffany st
 ained glass windows. Special guests include Drumdala\, the immersive percu
 ssion project by Richard Sherwood\, and Japanese Taiko. Taiko brings a com
 manding presence to the stage\, uniting movement\, rhythm\, and spirit. Th
 is spring\, Taiko Drummer David Gonzalez joins VOENA\, carrying the legacy
  and wisdom of Grandmaster Seiichi Tanaka\, the father of taiko in America
 . A respected local Taiko artist\, David has appeared in films such as Ret
 urn of the Jedi and performed at renowned venues including Zellerbach Hall
  and Carnegie Hall. The Taiko performance is further enriched by Heidi Var
 ian\, a highly regarded Taiko artist and author of The Way of Taiko. Heidi
 's deep understanding of Taiko's cultural significance and her mastery of 
 the art form adds a special layer to the performance\, creating an unforge
 ttable experience for the audience. VOENA's mission… Uniting the world w
 ith children's voices\, shines through as they bring global music traditio
 ns to life in one of the oldest Navy chapels on the West Coast. Tickets: $
 50 Reserved Seating \\(First 3 Rows\\) $40 General Seating
LOCATION:St. Peter&'s Chapel
URL:https://www.voena.org/concerts/2026/5/3/freedom
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
