BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lifespan of a Fact
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T152500
UID:250804zd-hnFVGIUG_ta2POKE8uA
DESCRIPTION:**Truth or Spin? The Fight over Facts.**\n\n***“Designed for
  laughs\, but the play has a provocative undercurrent regarding issues tha
 t make it a compelling piece of theatre.”* —Cincinnati CityBeat**\n\n*
 **The Lifespan of a Fact* is a critically acclaimed Broadway play that del
 ves into the contentious realm where truth and storytelling intersect. The
  narrative centers on Emily Penrose\, the exacting editor-in-chief of a pr
 estigious magazine\, who assigns Jim Fingal\, an ambitious young fact-chec
 ker\, to verify a groundbreaking essay by renowned author John D’Agata. 
 As Jim meticulously scrutinizes the piece\, he discovers numerous embellis
 hments\, igniting a fierce debate over the boundaries of factual accuracy 
 versus creative license. This fast-paced\, blistering comedy offers a time
 ly exploration of the high-stakes world of publishing\, where the quest fo
 r truth becomes a battleground of wit\, ethics\, and editorial judgment.**
 \n\n**The play has been lauded for its sharp dialogue and thought-provokin
 g themes\, prompting audiences to question: In storytelling\, how far can 
 one go before the facts become fiction?**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturda
 ys @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: 85 mins\, no inter
 mission\n\nThursdays Adult $33 Fri/Sat Eve Adult $39.95\; Senior $36.95\; 
 Under 18 $26.95 Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $47.95\; Senior $44.95 \\*All prices
  include fees (707) 523-4185\n\n**boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/lifespan-of-a-fact/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michelle Lambert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260510T000000
UID:260331E126u65vDEeggIxlMVSUzQ
DESCRIPTION:Join Michelle at the Larson Family Winery for a Mother's Day B
 runch event! It's fun for the entire family and of course mom! Beautiful c
 ountry winery in the Sonoma Valley. More info available here: https://lars
 onfamilywinery.com/upcoming-events/\n\nBay Area breakout artist Michelle L
 ambert delivers a fun\, high-energy show filled with edgy\, heartfelt orig
 inal music\, infectious pop hooks\, and unstoppable charisma. Fresh off a 
 successful 40-date tour across the Western states last year\, Michelle cap
 tivates audiences with soaring vocals\, dynamic violin solos\, and vibrant
  energy that radiates through the crowd. Her electrifying performances cre
 ate an unforgettable live experience that will have you dancing\, smiling\
 , and celebrating all night long.\n\nRaised in Northern California and tra
 ined at the prestigious Berklee College of Music\, Michelle Lambert has fo
 rged her own path as a fearless\, independent pop artist. She has topped t
 he charts of Indie Radio with her original songs and was featured in the S
 an Francisco Giants’ City Connect Campaign as a notable Bay Area artist.
  Michelle cut her teeth performing and writing in the competitive music sc
 enes of Nashville and Los Angeles before returning to the Bay Area to tour
  with her own thriving career. Known for her powerful vocals\, masterful v
 iolin playing\, and bold\, colorful costumes\, Michelle pairs striking vis
 uals with raw emotional storytelling—embodying creativity\, resilience\,
  and the adventure of chasing your dreams. For more info on Michelle visit
 : https://www.michellelambert.com
LOCATION:Larson Family Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108145732?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
