DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T083000
UID:260405W4zPl-gMekqsEw8uXj9XFg
DESCRIPTION:The Wine Sales Symposium is an in-person conference designed f
 or winery owners\, sales leaders\, marketing executives\, and decision-mak
 ers focused on driving revenue in an increasingly complex marketplace.\n\n
 The 2026 program confronts the realities reshaping wine sales today. From 
 artificial intelligence influencing brand visibility and purchasing decisi
 ons\, to evolving wine club retention strategies\, shifting distribution d
 ynamics\, and the redefinition of hospitality experiences\, this year’s 
 sessions focus on what wineries must understand and act on\, to remain com
 petitive.
LOCATION:DoubleTree by Hilton Hotel Sonoma Wine Country
URL:https://winesalessymposium.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family Art Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T170000
UID:260401a3jP9KhJH0Gvshud1VDXug
DESCRIPTION:4 - 18\\+ yrs Adult participation optional Class Experience To
 gether\, we will breathe and enjoy the feel of our hands creating with col
 orful textural materials. This class is designed for littles ones and thei
 r families to unwind and decompress in the late afternoon and enjoy proces
 s art. We will create with a variety of materials that will be set out in 
 an open ended\, Reggio Emelia style where students are offered invitations
  to play with the materials. We will explore different themes such as pain
 ting with acrylic or tempera\; do collages with various types of paper and
  mixed media\; practice sculpture\; or just make creative art with recycle
 d materials. The only assignment is to play and explore with colors\, shap
 es\, and textures\, with no messy clean-up at home! "Play is a key compone
 nt of the arts and aesthetics in myriad ways. Art and play are like two si
 des of the same coin\, with play being a part of artistic expression\, ima
 gination\, creativity\, and curiosity." - Susan Magsamen\,  Your Brain on 
 Art: How the Arts Transform Us Amanda Rose Hopkins has a Bachelor of Fine 
 Arts from UC Santa Cruz and thereafter she worked as an apprentice artist 
 at the Sarnath International Nyingma Institute\, near Varanasi\, India. Sh
 e has been working with children since 2009. She completed a multiple subj
 ect teaching credential program and has worked locally at Sunridge Charter
  School\, The REACH School\, Sebastopol Center for the Arts and Santa Rosa
  Junior College. She has studied multicultural education\, Positive Discip
 line\, Toolbox and child development. Notes Land of the Good Members get 2
 0% \\(!\\) off this class using code: 2026member To utilize the discount\,
  please first activate a membership or email us at hello@landofthegood.com
  if you need help subscribing! Class Requirements Students need to be full
 y potty-trained and able to communicate/navigate self-care needs. What you
 'll learn Students will be exposed to methods of painting Various types of
  paintbrushes Acrylic painting Tempera painting Oil pastel drawing Collage
  Types of adhesives and their uses Sculptural techniques Recycled art Samp
 le Class Format 3:15pm - 5:00pm\; late drop-off or early pick-up are fine 
 as this is an open-art lab and children may have varying capacity. Parents
  or other supervising adults are welcome to stay and participate or enjoy 
 tea & coffee and use the high-speed internet/cowork during class time. Ple
 ase pick up promptly by 5pm. Other Things To Know Adult Participation Opti
 onal. One adult View more
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Junior College
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/family-art-lab/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T170000
UID:260330kH3aajnUqUi5jjvS7ByU-Q
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Robyn Hitchcock
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T000000
UID:2603270EryhyDfJECiysVB16Z-jQ
DESCRIPTION:Robyn Hitchcock is one of England's most enduring contemporary
  singer/songwriters and live performers. A surrealist poet\, talented guit
 arist\, cult artist and musician's musician\, Hitchcock is among alternati
 ve rock's father figures and is the closest thing the genre has to a Bob D
 ylan \\(not coincidentally his biggest musical inspiration\\).\n\nSince fo
 unding the art-rock band The Soft Boys in 1976\, Robyn has recorded more t
 han 20 albums as well as starred in ‘Storefront Hitchcock’ an in conce
 rt film recorded in New York and directed by Jonathan Demme. \n\nBlending 
 folk and psychedelia with a wry British nihilism\, Robyn describes his son
 gs as ‘paintings you can listen to’. His most recent album is self-tit
 led and marks his 21st release as a solo artist. Out on April 21 2017\, th
 e album is produced by Brendan Benson \\(The Raconteurs\\). Hitchcock desc
 ribes it as a "ecstatic work of negativity with nary a dreary groove." \n\
 nIt has received rave reviews from UNCUT\, Rolling Stone\, Paste\, Tidal a
 nd more. \n\n"A gifted melodist\, Hitchcock nests engaging lyrics in some 
 of the most bracing\, rainbow-hued pop this side of Revolver. He wrests in
 spiration not from ordinary life but from extraordinary imaginings..." - R
 olling Stone\n\n"These 10 gems slither\, rock\, roll\, glide and shapeshif
 t\, coalescing around Hitchcock’s typically anxious\, strained but strik
 ing and immediately identifiable vocals." - American Songwriter\n\n"Belove
 d of everyone from Led Zeppelin to REM\, Hitchcock has only enhanced his s
 tatus with this wonderful outing." - Hot Press\n\n"Witty\, moving and seri
 ously catchy\, Robyn Hitchcock is a glorious return for a man who wasn’t
  really gone in the first place." - Paste Magazine
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108042012?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Pottery on the Wheel\; Advanced
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T210000
UID:260325ZZGrZJlLfE2rmECyNgazZg
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesdays\, April 1 – May 20\, 2026 6:00 PM –
  9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\n
 Intermediate and Advanced\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Extended Classes
 \n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n17\\+\n\n$265 – Registration Cost $30 – Materials Fe
 e $295 – Total Registration Cost\n\nA continuation of our intermediate c
 ourse\, this upper level / advanced course will help you hone your throwin
 g skills in the studio.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nThis session is designed for
  people who have already taken multiple wheel throwing courses. A continua
 tion of our intermediate course\, this upper level / advanced course will 
 help you hone your throwing skills through more complex demos\, and nuance
 d approaches to technical throwing. In this 8 week course\, students will 
 dive deep into developing their own unique voice as they build a technical
  toolset for the independent maker. In addition to throwing\, surface deco
 ration techniques will be explored as well as the opportunity to experimen
 t with different clay bodies. With your 8 week class registration\, studen
 ts receive the opportunity to purchase a studio pass for ½ off during the
  duration of their class. Sign ups for membership will be included in your
  preclass email
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/wednesday-pottery-on-the-wh
 eel-advanced/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quench at Copia: The Mount "Crushmore" of American Wine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T183000
UID:2603244GaZEJdwjEucPm2t0nl5Qw
DESCRIPTION:Be a part of the LIVE studio audience in the Napa Valley Vintn
 ers Theatre at the CIA at Copia! Master Sommelier Andrea Immer Robinson ta
 kes her newest podcast series\, Quench at Copia\, to another level with sp
 ecial guest experts and YOU in the audience!\n\nThis month\, Andrea will b
 e taking us through the renowned Judgment of Paris of 1976 as part of our 
 50th Anniversary Celebration\, when Napa Valley became a global icon. You'
 ll taste the winning wines from the original competition along with comple
 mentary bites and a sample dish from The Grove restaurant.\n\n**This is no
 t a standard wine tasting. This is a masterclass in gastronomy.**\n\nWhile
  Napa offers hundreds of tasting experiences throughout the Valley\, it is
  almost unheard of to have direct\, intimate access to talent of this cali
 ber in a single evening. This is your opportunity to bypass the standard t
 asting room script and learn directly from seasoned hospitality profession
 als.\n\nMore details to follow.
LOCATION:CIA at Copia
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/quench-at-copia-the-mount-crushmore-of-am
 erican-wine-tickets-1985410580492?aff=oddtdtcreator&keep_tld=true
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: The Poetic Landscape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260513T180000
UID:260318vLiSjOHprEyLbR0mSMIdvw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  3/13/26\n\n**APRIL EXHIBIT: THE 
 POETIC LANDSCAPE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  March 30  – April 26\, 2026\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, APRIL 4\, 2026\, 3-5 pm: Join us to meet KAREN MILL
 ER and PHYLLIS RAPP\;  celebrate the show and enjoy a poetry reading by f
 eatured guest\, Linda Loveland Reid\, gallery artist and published author.
   Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthly drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Karen Miller\,** presents **The Poetic Landscape\,** pa
 stel paintings that convey Miller’s personal experience in connecting wi
 th the intrinsic beauty of natural places. In these pieces\, color\, fluid
  shapes and rhythmic design combine to create an uplifting mood – a true
  poetic interlude.  Evoking a happy mood\, “Geyserville Sunflowers\,”
  turning to the sun by nature\, joyfully dance in its luminescence. By the
  river’s edge\, concentric reflections conjure a calm sense of wellbeing
  in “Fetch.”  The viewer feels welcomed by a warm embrace entering a 
 shaded secret spot in “September Trellis.”  Focused on local scenes\,
  these works truly hone in on the stunning landscape out our doors.  Mill
 er remarked “ As I contemplate the very real places of beauty surroundin
 g us\, I try to express my painterly response in hopes it will engender re
 cognition by the viewers.” \n\nMeet the artist: Miller will be hosting 
 the Gallery on March 30\, April 5 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n The Stai
 rway Smallworks Showcase features **Phyllis Rapp’s Magic Moments\,** a c
 ollection of watercolors that create an atmosphere that is both introspect
 ive and magical.  Familiar domestic scenes are transformed as humans inte
 ract with animals and birds in floral settings.  In “Silent Watcher” 
 the red-headed young woman’s green eyes lock onto ours as she stares ahe
 ad\, flanked by her avian companion.  Experiencing these works is a like 
 taking a mini-step on the wild side\, an exciting and fun experience.\n\nM
 eet the artist: Rapp will be hosting the Gallery on March 30 and April 10 
 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\
 , April 2\, 5 – 6 pm.  The theme for the 2026 kickoff event is Bouquets
  to Art.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is
  a community event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries p
 articipating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Cente
 r Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 
 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Con
 tact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
